 # With presence available, the completion is held until somebody is plainly
-# back at the terminal instead of being timed out blind. The ceiling exists
-# because an unattended Mac would otherwise flash green until morning, and
-# because a completion nobody acknowledged in five minutes has stopped being
-# news and started being wallpaper.
-COMPLETION_HOLD_MAX_SECONDS = 300.0
+# back at the terminal. Zero means there is no ceiling at all: only a click, a
+# scroll or a keystroke retires it.
+#
+# This was 300s, on the reasoning that an unattended Mac would otherwise flash
+# green until morning. But flashing green until morning is the correct
+# behaviour - the run did finish, nobody has been told, and the moment the
+# ceiling is reached is precisely the moment the signal was doing its job.
+# Retiring news because it is old only guarantees that the completions you
+# most needed to hear about are the ones you never see.
+COMPLETION_HOLD_MAX_SECONDS = 0.0
 
 # Presence is sampled far faster than the 15s status refresh so that sitting
 # down clears the completion within a second rather than a quarter-minute.
