-        rows = list(statuses)
+        Subagent rows are dropped first, for the same reason every other reader
+        of these rows drops them - `aggregate_status`, `menu_statuses`,
+        `CompletionWatcher` and `active_signals_for` all do. A subagent is an
+        implementation detail of the turn that spawned it: it cannot be
+        prompted, it is not addressable from the menu, and it routinely
+        orphans mid-run when its parent moves on. A failure inside one is the
+        parent's to handle, and the parent reports its own outcome.
+
+        The latch was the single reader that kept them, and it is the one with
+        absolute precedence over the display. So one dead subagent held the
+        device red over a session that had long since finished successfully,
+        with nothing the user could do about it - a prompt to the parent only
+        reaches the child while both rows are still present and lineage is
+        intact.
